// examples/hydramodem/quantum.exsc -- what the modem carries: spec §5.2's
// DeModFrame, the 17-byte DCF quantum, and the CRC HydraModem appends to it.
// Pure: no `poscit`, no capability, no `initium`.
//
// The declaration is §5.2's worked example verbatim, as tests/programs/
// forma/ declares it: there is no module system yet to import §14 entry
// 23's. The modem never reads a field -- it takes the frame's seventeen
// bytes, `f sicut acies<u8, 17>` -- so the type is here for the drivers,
// which write each frame as a struct literal, every field named.

@transitus
publica structura DeModFrame {
    signum:  u8               // 0xD3, the first validity gate
    versio:  u4               // packs MSB-first with genus
    genus:   u4               // frame type
    numerus: u16:maior
    fons:    u16:maior
    meta:    u16:maior
    onus:    u32:maior
    tempus:  u24:maior        // 24-bit microsecond offset
    cursus:  u16:maior        // CRC-16/CCITT-FALSE over bytes 0..14
}

// CRC-16/CCITT-FALSE over b[0..n): init 0xFFFF, polynomial 0x1021, no
// reflection, no final xor -- hydra_crc.c, and entry 23's `redundantia`
// unchanged. `c sursum 1` discards the bit shifted past the top (spec §5.4),
// so there is no mask; `c ge 0x8000` reads that bit before it goes.
//
// HydraModem computes it over all SEVENTEEN bytes (hydra_frame.c,
// build_data_bits), cursus included. For a valid frame that is the CRC of a
// word followed by its own CRC, which for this CRC is always 0x0000 -- so on
// every valid frame the sixteen bits it appends are zeros. It is computed
// here all the same: the modem does not know the frame is valid, and an
// invalid one gets a nonzero CRC.
publica functio redundantia(b: acies<u8, 17>, n: mensura) -> u16 {
    mutabilis c: u16 = 0xffff;
    per i in 0..n {
        c = c aut ((b[i] sicut u16) sursum 8);
        per k in 0..8 {
            si c ge 0x8000 {
                c = (c sursum 1) aut 0x1021;
            } aliter {
                c = c sursum 1;
            }
        }
    }
    redde c;
}
